# Playwright Login Automation Tests

The project currently includes tests for:

- login scenarios on the Expand Testing practice website
- input field scenarios on QA Playground

More test suites will be added gradually as new practice pages are covered.

The tests are written in Python using Playwright and Pytest.

## Test coverage for Login

The project covers the main login scenarios:

- successful login with valid credentials
- login by pressing the Enter key
- keyboard navigation using Tab
- successful login after a failed attempt
- invalid username
- invalid password
- empty credentials
- empty username or password
- whitespace-only values
- credentials with incorrect letter case
- username with leading and trailing spaces
- long username
- username with special characters

Negative scenarios are implemented using `pytest.mark.parametrize` to avoid duplicated test code.

## Project approach

- A session-scoped fixture starts the browser once for the test session.
- A new browser page is created for every test to keep tests isolated.
- Repeated login actions are moved to a reusable helper function.
- Playwright assertions are used to verify URLs, messages, element visibility, and keyboard focus.
- Tests run in Chromium in headless mode.

## Test coverage for QA Playground Input Fields

The project also includes automated tests for the QA Playground Input Fields page:

https://qaplayground.com/practice/input-fields

Current and planned coverage includes:

- typing text into an input field
- submitting the typed value
- checking that the result matches the entered value
- appending text to an existing value
- reading a predefined input value
- clearing an input field
- checking disabled input behavior
- checking readonly input behavior

Additional tests for this page and other QA Playground practice sections will be added later.
## Installation

```bash
pip install pytest playwright pytest-html
playwright install chromium

## Run tests

Run login tests:
```bash
pytest tests/test_expandtesting_login.py --html=reports/test_expandtesting_login.html
pytest tests/test_qaplayground_input_field.py --html=reports/test_qaplayground_input_field.html